## 2. Generation / derivation code

**`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** — invoked during owner save (lines 254-262):
```java
if (owner.isNew() && owner.getCustomerCode() == null) {
    owner.setCustomerCode(generateCustomerCode(owner));
}
if (owner.isNew()) {
    owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner));
}
if (owner.getMembershipNumber() == null) {
    owner.setMembershipNumber(generateMembershipNumber(owner));
}
```

`generateCustomerCode` (lines 339-344) — format `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, LAST3 = upper-cased first 3 letters of last name, NNNN = (owner count + 1) zero-padded to 4 digits:
```java
private String generateCustomerCode(Owner owner) {
    String lastName = owner.getLastName();
    String last3 = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase();
    long sequence = ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1L;
    return String.format("%s-%04d", last3, sequence);
}
```
Note: no city prefix. This is what the acceptance test's regex contradicts (see section 4).

`generateMembershipNumber` (lines 350-353) — format `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of registration year:
```java
private String generateMembershipNumber(Owner owner) {
    String yy = String.format("%02d", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
    return String.format("%s-M%s", owner.getCustomerCode(), yy);
}
```

**`OwnerMapper.toMembershipTier`** (lines 52-56) — derives read-only `membershipTier` on the DTO (not stored):
```java
default String toMembershipTier(Owner owner) {
    boolean uniqueName = Integer.valueOf(0).equals(owner.getNamesakeCount());
    boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();
    return uniqueName && hasEmail ? "SILVER" : "BRONZE";
}
```
Wired via `@Mapping(target = "membershipTier", expression = "java(toMembershipTier(owner))")` on `toOwnerDto`. The mapper also derives `displayName` and `initials`.

---

## 3. Entity / model classes

**`Owner.java`** (`@Entity`, table `owners`) extends **`Person`**. Fields relevant here:
- `customerCode` (`@Column(name = "customer_code")`, line 60) — stored
- `membershipNumber` (`@Column(name = "membership_number")`, line 63) — stored
- `namesakeCount` (`namesake_count`) — feeds membershipTier
- `householdId`, `city` (`@NotEmpty`), `address` (`@NotEmpty`), `telephone` (`@Pattern` E.164), `email` (`@Email`), `registrationDate`, `pets`, transient `sharesHousehold`

**`Person.java`** (`@MappedSuperclass`) provides `firstName` and `lastName` (both `@NotEmpty`), used by the generators. `membershipTier` is a DTO-only field (not on the entity).

DB column widths differ slightly across dialects: `customer_code VARCHAR(20)` and `membership_number VARCHAR(30)` in h2/hsqldb/mysql; postgres uses `membership_number TEXT`.

---

## 4. Tests

Only one test asserts these values: **`AcceptanceTest.java`**:
```java
/** customer-code-city: Change the customerCode format to '<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>' ... */
@Test
void coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix() throws Exception {
    int id = createOwnerOk(ownerNode());
    JsonNode n = fetchOwner(id);
    assertTrue(n.get("customerCode").asText().matches("[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}")); // <CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>
}
```
This expects three uppercase-letter/dash segments ending in 4 digits, i.e. a **city prefix** the current `generateCustomerCode` does not produce — the implementation emits `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (one letter segment + digits). As written, this test would fail against the current code; it appears to describe a pending change ("customer-code-city: Change the customerCode format...").

**`AcceptanceBase.java`** is the shared harness: posts to `POST /api/owners`, reads back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, uses `@Transactional` rollback, `@WithMockUser(... OWNER_ADMIN ...)`. `ownerNode()` builds a fully-valid unique owner (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone — no email, so its membershipTier would be BRONZE). Its class javadoc mentions the "membership number" count rule but contains no membership assertions. It also provides generic helpers (`sha256hex`, `luhn`, city/region/postcode tables) not specific to customerCode.

No other unit/integration tests reference customerCode, membershipNumber, or membershipTier.

---

## 5. Build system & running tests

- **Maven** only: `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` with wrapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw` (and `mvnw.cmd`). No Gradle files present.
- Run full suite: `./mvnw test`
- Run just the acceptance test: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`
- Full verify (if integration phases apply): `./mvnw verify`

The app uses an OpenAPI-generated DTO layer (`openapi.yml` → `OwnerDto`/`OwnerFieldsDto`) and MapStruct mappers, so a `./mvnw` build also triggers code generation before compiling the mapper that references `membershipTier`.

